Feature: Radio calibration
  F2 opens a wizard that learns your radio's sticks by watching you move them. While it is
  open the sticks and buttons don't fly the plane, so sweeping the throttle doesn't throw it.

  Expectation: Calibrate opens the wizard
    Given the calibration wizard is closed
    When the pilot presses calibrate
    Then the calibration wizard is open

  Expectation: Calibrate again closes the wizard
    Given the calibration wizard is open
    When the pilot presses calibrate
    Then the calibration wizard is closed

  Expectation: The wizard holds the plane while you sweep the throttle
    Overrides: Throttle up throws the plane
    Given the aircraft is in hand
    And the calibration wizard is open
    When the throttle is above 55 %
    Then the aircraft is in hand

  Expectation: The wizard ignores the launch button
    Overrides: The launch button throws the plane
    Given the aircraft is in hand
    And the calibration wizard is open
    When the pilot presses launch
    Then the aircraft is in hand
